/*
    Time Intelligence calculation group (requirement #3).
    Fiscal year runs April-March. Applies to ANY base measure (Net Revenue,
    Gross Sales, Margin, ...) without duplicating measures per period type.

    Created in Tabular Editor / via TMDL, not plain DAX in a measure — shown
    here as the calculation items that make up the group.

    Calculation Group: "Time Intelligence"
    Precedence: 10
    Column: "Time Calculation" (what shows in the field list / slicer)
*/

-- Prerequisite: Dim Date must have FiscalYear, FiscalMonthNumber (1=April) columns,
-- and be marked as the model's Date Table with Date Table [Date] = 'Dim Date'[Date].

-- Calculation Item: "Current" (the base case, no transformation)
SELECTEDMEASURE ()

-- Calculation Item: "YTD" (fiscal, not calendar)
CALCULATE (
    SELECTEDMEASURE (),
    DATESYTD ( 'Dim Date'[Date], "3/31" )   -- FY ends March 31
)

-- Calculation Item: "PY" (prior fiscal year, same period)
CALCULATE (
    SELECTEDMEASURE (),
    DATEADD ( 'Dim Date'[Date], -1, YEAR )
)

-- Calculation Item: "YoY %"
VAR CurrentValue = SELECTEDMEASURE ()
VAR PriorValue =
    CALCULATE ( SELECTEDMEASURE (), DATEADD ( 'Dim Date'[Date], -1, YEAR ) )
RETURN
    DIVIDE ( CurrentValue - PriorValue, PriorValue )

-- Calculation Item: "Rolling 12M"
CALCULATE (
    SELECTEDMEASURE (),
    DATESINPERIOD ( 'Dim Date'[Date], MAX ( 'Dim Date'[Date] ), -12, MONTH )
)

/*
    Usage in a report: drop [Net Revenue] on a visual, then slice by the
    "Time Calculation" column from this calculation group. Switching the
    slicer between Current/YTD/PY/YoY %/Rolling 12M applies to whichever base
    measure is on the visual — Net Revenue, Gross Sales, Margin, all of them —
    with zero extra measures authored.

    This is what replaces the 50-duplicated-measures anti-pattern
    (Net Revenue YTD, Gross Sales YTD, Margin YTD, Net Revenue PY, ... x5
    measures x 5 time periods = 25+ measures, growing with every new base
    measure). With a calculation group it's 5 base measures + 5 calculation
    items, period, and every future base measure inherits the group for free.
*/
